hi this is Mario with Mario's math  tutoring coming to you with another math  video to help you boost your score in  your math class improve your  understanding and hopefully make  learning math a lot less stressful so in  this video what we're going to talk  about is how to find the area of  trapezoids okay so what exactly is a  trapezoid well a trapezoid is a  quadrilateral meaning it has four sides  with one pair of opposite sides parallel  okay so you can see that these are  parallel but these are not parallel okay  and when you find the area what you do  is you take one-half times the height  the height is the perpendicular distance  between these two parallel sides which  are referred to as the bases and then  you multiply times the sum of the two  bases so it's base one plus base two  times the height times one-half and that  gives you the area of the trapezoid so  let's look at some examples and you'll  get a sense of how this works so in this  one here you can see here's our parallel  sides these are going to be our bases  all we have to do is go ahead and  substitute we have one half the height  is 4 and the two bases are going to be 8  and 12 so we just have to add those  together so that's gonna be 20 times 1/2  is 10 times 4 is 40 so this is going to  be 40 units squared and that's the exact  area of the trapezoid okay let's take a  look at another example now in this  example it's a little bit more  challenging right we know that base 1 we  don't know what Beast 2 is and we don't  know what the height is but they give us  a little clue they tell us that this  angle here is 45 degrees so if you know  your 45-45-90 triangles it's going to be  easy to figure out they're in the ratio  of X X X square root of 2 okay if you  want you can check out my video on the  special right triangles I'll have a link  for that up above but basically if this  is 5 root 2 that tells us that this side  is going to be 5 this side here is going  to be 5 this is going to be 8 see how  we've sectioned this off into a  rectangle so the opposite sides are  congruent so that means that this whole  base here is going to be 13 ok  and now we can use our area formula so  it's going to be area equals  1/2 times the height which is 5 times  the sum of the bases which is going to  be 13 plus 8 okay so if we go and  simplify that down what do we get we've  got 13 plus 8 which is 21 okay times 5  which is 105 divided by 2 which is 52  point five right so 52 point 5 units  squared that's going to give us an area  of the trapezoid so I hope you enjoyed  this video I hope you learned something  go ahead and subscribe to the channel  check out some of my past videos and  I've got more videos like this coming  for you so I'll talk to you in the next  video I'll talk to you soon
 

